=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
title: a codemod's __testfixtures__ output is data beside the tests, not a test
origin: issue #175 bound — Jest's defaults collect __tests__/ and spec/test names, not neighbouring fixture directories; a codemod that rewrites toBe(true) into toBeTruthy() legitimately changes its expected output this way
=== before: transforms/__testfixtures__/truthy-matchers.output.js ===
test("ready", () => {
  expect(isReady()).toBe(true);
});
=== after: transforms/__testfixtures__/truthy-matchers.output.js ===
test("ready", () => {
  expect(isReady()).toBeTruthy();
});
=== expect ===
[]
